      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>Do field reports hold personal data?</h3><p>Usually yes. A name, an address linked to a person, or a photo of a person is personal data. It does not matter if it is on paper or digital.</p><h3>Must a small firm register with the Information Commission?</h3><p>Almost all commercial firms must. The fee is £40 a year for a small organisation. Not registering is a criminal offence. Check at <a href=\"https://ico.org.uk\">ico.org.uk</a>.</p><h3>How long should I keep field reports?</h3><p>No longer than you need. Legal records have a minimum. Contract records are usually kept six years. Write a retention policy.</p><h3>Does EU or UK hosting matter?</h3><p>UK GDPR limits sending data outside the UK without safeguards. EU hosting meets both UK and EU rules. Quickler uses Hetzner servers in Germany. Registered with the Information Commission ZC124993. DPA on request.</p>"
